WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:04.255
- [Both] I just got a Tumblr.

00:00:04.255 --> 00:00:06.331
I do not understand Tumblr.

00:00:06.331 --> 00:00:07.680
- Don't really know what a 'note' is.

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:09.362
- Don't really like the
feeling of being followed.

00:00:09.362 --> 00:00:10.535
- [Both] By strangers.

00:00:10.535 --> 00:00:12.033
- Why do they call them 'followers'?

00:00:12.033 --> 00:00:13.414
- Can't we just be friends?

00:00:13.414 --> 00:00:16.317
- [Both] I have 81
followers, mostly strangers,

00:00:16.317 --> 00:00:18.116
and they send me messages that say,

00:00:18.116 --> 00:00:19.834
- Thanks for the reblog, but,

00:00:19.834 --> 00:00:22.202
- [Both] What's with all that
feminist spam on your feed?

00:00:22.202 --> 00:00:23.038
- I did not respond.

00:00:23.038 --> 00:00:24.826
- You were so pretty with your long hair.

00:00:24.826 --> 00:00:26.771
- [Both] Did you really
need a queer haircut?

00:00:26.771 --> 00:00:28.170
- I did not respond.

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:29.551
- My grandmother, who's
been taking care of me

00:00:29.551 --> 00:00:31.246
since I was a kid, found out I'm gay.

00:00:31.246 --> 00:00:34.693
But she keeps telling me I'm
just going through a phase.

00:00:34.693 --> 00:00:37.028
It's really getting to
me, what should I do?

00:00:37.028 --> 00:00:39.244
- [Both] P.S., I like your poetry.

00:00:40.364 --> 00:00:43.319
Phase, noun: a distinct
period in a process

00:00:43.319 --> 00:00:44.678
of change or development.

00:00:44.678 --> 00:00:46.396
- I am seven years old
and leaving a play date

00:00:46.396 --> 00:00:47.371
from Samantha's house.

00:00:47.371 --> 00:00:48.555
I give her a kiss on the cheek

00:00:48.555 --> 00:00:50.552
and both of our mothers swoon.

00:00:50.552 --> 00:00:52.060
I am seven years old
and leaving a play date

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:53.152
from Michael's house.

00:00:53.152 --> 00:00:55.659
I give him a kiss on the
cheek, and his mother says,

00:00:55.659 --> 00:00:57.074
- [Both] Now, that's enough of.

00:00:57.074 --> 00:01:00.679
Phase, verb: to introduce
in gradual stages.

00:01:00.679 --> 00:01:03.582
- I was 22 years old when
I began dating a woman

00:01:03.582 --> 00:01:04.998
for the first time.

00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:07.946
She pulled me in from the
starless, darkness I'd been

00:01:07.946 --> 00:01:10.802
drifting through and I
watched as all my insecurities

00:01:10.802 --> 00:01:12.939
burned up in her atmosphere.

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:13.879
Her name is,

00:01:13.879 --> 00:01:17.338
- [Both] Phase, verb: to
remove in gradual stages.

00:01:17.338 --> 00:01:18.836
- In high school, I knew this painter.

00:01:18.836 --> 00:01:21.413
A cocksure comet with a confident,

00:01:21.413 --> 00:01:24.303
smarter-than-you smile that
showed no signs of burning out.

00:01:24.303 --> 00:01:27.009
A hopeful romantic, who
always wanted to exchange

00:01:27.009 --> 00:01:31.260
portraits for poems, and I'm
afraid if I write him one now,

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:33.338
it will sound too much
like the suicide note

00:01:33.338 --> 00:01:36.292
that he did not leave, signed,

00:01:36.292 --> 00:01:40.257
- [Both] Phase, verb, the
process of waxing and waning.

00:01:40.257 --> 00:01:42.683
- [Girl] It takes the moon 29 days

00:01:42.683 --> 00:01:44.541
to orbit around the Earth.

00:01:44.541 --> 00:01:46.817
- [Both] Appearing to us only in fractions

00:01:46.817 --> 00:01:48.023
of it's full self.

00:01:48.023 --> 00:01:50.462
Phase, verb, to illuminate the darkness.

00:01:50.462 --> 00:01:53.109
- And what are we really ever doing?

00:01:53.109 --> 00:01:55.848
- [Both] If not constantly
trying to find a light,

00:01:55.848 --> 00:01:58.426
when they tell you your
love is just a phase,

00:01:58.426 --> 00:02:01.084
- Tell them you do not
like the word 'just.'

00:02:01.084 --> 00:02:03.185
- [Both] You are not 'just' anything.

00:02:03.185 --> 00:02:06.587
- Do not bury your demons on
the dark side of the moon.

00:02:06.587 --> 00:02:09.268
- [Both] Instead, phase
hate out of your sky.

00:02:09.268 --> 00:02:10.928
When they treat your love like an eclipse,

00:02:10.928 --> 00:02:12.484
- [Boy] Like it means learning to live

00:02:12.484 --> 00:02:14.144
in someone else's shadow.

00:02:14.144 --> 00:02:16.466
- [Girl] Like it deserves
to be black hole swallowed

00:02:16.466 --> 00:02:18.985
because it burns too bright to look at.

00:02:18.985 --> 00:02:20.123
- [Both] Do not let them.

00:02:20.123 --> 00:02:21.423
- Do not align yourself with

00:02:21.423 --> 00:02:23.664
someone else's access of expectation.

00:02:23.664 --> 00:02:25.649
- Do not fight your own pull.

00:02:25.649 --> 00:02:27.529
- [Both] Trust in your own gravity.

00:02:27.529 --> 00:02:30.884
We are closer to the stars
than they will ever be.

00:02:30.884 --> 00:02:33.287
- And if anyone ever tries to tell you

00:02:33.287 --> 00:02:35.389
that you love wrong.

00:02:35.389 --> 00:02:38.546
- If anyone waits for you to
backwards become yourself.

00:02:38.546 --> 00:02:40.624
- [Both] Treats your
queerness as anything other

00:02:40.624 --> 00:02:43.549
than the infinite universe
of beautiful possibilities

00:02:43.549 --> 00:02:45.721
that it is, tell them that you're sorry

00:02:45.721 --> 00:02:47.368
that they'd rather live in darkness

00:02:47.368 --> 00:02:49.308
than learn to love your light,

00:02:49.308 --> 00:02:51.781
learn to love your flicker,
flash of radiation,

00:02:51.781 --> 00:02:53.963
learn to love you full moon.

00:02:54.943 --> 00:02:56.607
- [Girl] And even on
the days when you hang

00:02:56.607 --> 00:02:58.673
just a sliver in the sky.

00:02:58.673 --> 00:03:01.889
- [Boy] When it feels like
you're holding on for dear life,

00:03:01.889 --> 00:03:05.151
to this rock, like you
are in a death-grip tango

00:03:05.151 --> 00:03:06.253
with the sun.

00:03:07.133 --> 00:03:08.074
- [Both] Hold on.

00:03:08.074 --> 00:03:11.417
Because I've seen people
I love starve themselves

00:03:11.417 --> 00:03:13.298
out of the sky.

00:03:13.298 --> 00:03:15.487
- Her name is Sarah.

00:03:16.537 --> 00:03:19.195
- Signed, Andrew.

00:03:19.195 --> 00:03:22.713
- [Girl] My starry-eyed girl
and her constellation kisses.

00:03:22.713 --> 00:03:26.550
- My man in the moon in his ghostly glow.

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:29.876
- [Both] I still don't understand Tumblr,

00:03:31.046 --> 00:03:33.214
but I consider us friends.

00:03:34.078 --> 00:03:36.922
Thank you for sending us
your secret satellite.

00:03:36.922 --> 00:03:39.970
We promise it did not get lost in space.

00:03:40.904 --> 00:03:45.904
P.S., we hear you, loud and clear.

00:03:46.163 --> 00:03:50.650
(slow, dramatic music)

